/// How likely a cash-on-delivery parcel is to come back unopened.
///
/// `TRUSTED` is not simply the bottom of the scale — it is reserved for a
/// customer with a delivery history the platform can read. A low score on no
/// evidence is `LOW`, because "we have no reason to worry" and "we have
/// watched her take eleven parcels" are different claims and only one of them
/// should buy a frictionless checkout.
enum CodRiskTier {
  TRUSTED
  LOW
  MEDIUM
  HIGH
}

/// What the platform asks for before it will send cash out on the road.
///
/// The ladder only ever goes up, and it never ends in a refusal to sell: the
/// top rung moves the money to a rail that does not put a courier's day at
/// risk, it does not turn the customer away.
enum CodAssurance {
  /// Place it exactly as she asked.
  NONE

  /// One code to the number on the order before the sellers are told to
  /// prepare it. Proves the number is live and that a human meant it.
  ORDER_CONFIRMATION

  /// Cash is not offered for this basket; it ships once it is paid for.
  PREPAYMENT
}

/// Where an order stands against the assurance its assessment demanded.
enum CodAssuranceState {
  NOT_REQUIRED
  PENDING
  SATISFIED
  /// The window closed with no code and no payment.
  ABANDONED
}

enum MediaType {
  image
  video

  /// A file that is read rather than looked at — a commercial register, a
  /// certificate. Only ever reachable through `MediaVisibility.PRIVATE`: the
  /// purposes that accept one are the document purposes, and a PDF where a
  /// product photograph was expected renders as a broken tile on every card
  /// that shows it.
  document

  /// A voice note. Gated the same way and for the same reason: a recording
  /// where a photograph belongs is a broken tile, and the only purpose that
  /// takes one today is a conversation.
  ///
  /// Duration lives on `MessageAttachment.durationMs`, measured by the
  /// recorder on the handset — reading it from the container would mean
  /// parsing an MP4 box tree for a number the client already knows exactly.
  audio
}

/// Who may fetch the bytes.
///
/// The distinction is not cosmetic: `governmentIdUrl` on a seller
/// verification is a photograph of a national ID card. Public assets are
/// served straight off disk by the reverse proxy; private ones are only ever
/// streamed through an authorised handler, and the two live in different
/// directory roots so a proxy misconfiguration cannot expose the second.
enum MediaVisibility {
  PUBLIC
  PRIVATE
}

/// An upload is a two-step affair: the bytes land first, the row that points
/// at them is written afterwards by whichever feature the caller was filling
/// in. Between those two moments the asset is PENDING and nothing references
/// it — a woman who picks a photo and then abandons the product form leaves
/// one behind. The sweeper deletes PENDING assets past their grace period,
/// which is only safe because ATTACHED is set the instant something points at
/// them.
enum MediaAssetStatus {
  PENDING
  ATTACHED
}

